graphCompiler.userPromptTemplate:
Compile AST to React Flow graph:
{astJSON}

Generate:
- Nodes with id, type, position, data
- Edges with proper handle references
- Field-level connections using output-{fieldId} and input-{fieldId}
- Node-level connections using node-source and node-target
- Edge IDs: edge_{source}_{sourceHandle}_{target}_{targetHandle}

Schema: {graphSchema}
Node catalog: {nodeCatalog}
Validation rules: {validationRules}

validator.userPromptTemplate:
Validate graph:
{graphJSON}

Check:
- Graph structure (DAG, no cycles)
- Node validity (types, configs, fields)
- Edge validity (endpoints, handles, types)
- Type compatibility
- Expression syntax

Validation rules: {validationRules}

Return: {valid: boolean, errors: [], warnings: []}

typeInferencer.userPromptTemplate:
Infer types for fields:
{fields}

Context:
{context}

Use type system:
{typeSystem}

Return fields with inferred types.

expressionParser.userPromptTemplate:
Parse expression:
{expression}

Available fields:
{inputFields}

Grammar:
- Field references: {{fieldName}}
- Operators: ==, !=, <, >, <=, >=, &&, ||, !
- Functions: count, sum, avg, min, max, concat, lower, upper
- Type conversion: STRING(), INT(), REAL(), DATE(), DATETIME()

Validate syntax and field references. Return: {valid: boolean, parsedExpression: {}, errors: []}
